The complete script now passes: all five prompt examples execute to the stated values, and the symbolic `kprove` run returns `#Top` with exit code 0. I’m adding one final guard that checks the AST embedded in the proof claim is exactly the regenerated `solution.mpy` term modulo formatting, so the proof cannot silently drift away from the submitted Python.
