Audit complete: **FAIL / NOT_LEGIT**.

The clean proof reaches `#Top` and is non-vacuous, but the generated semantics unsoundly maps Python floor division to truncating K division, enabling a demonstrably false claim to prove with `#Top`. The implementation also diverges from the canonical function for some negative integers.

Detailed review: [REVIEW.md](/audit-output/REVIEW.md)  
Reproducible artifacts: [evidence](/audit-output/evidence/)
diff --git a/REVIEW.md b/REVIEW.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d29466aa8f0691f55e50bd4596cffb19cf749433
